tags: calls, rate limit

A limit of the node: the most calls of one client in a window of time.

The value is an integer in calls. Example: 120. When a client passes the limit, the node refuses its calls for a time that the node selects.

The scope is the window in seconds, as text. Example: 60. It is not empty.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=calls
per=one client: the client_id of the caller; all the RPCs with client authentication count together
rule=When a client passes the limit, the node refuses its calls for a time that the node selects.
scope=the window, in seconds, base 10, as ASCII; not empty
unit=calls
